  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Churchill returns for his subsequent annual wellness visit, three weeks after his three-month stroke review. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. He is back at full work and gave a long speech without difficulty. He has had no falls, no further lightheadedness since amlodipine was reduced, and no new neurological symptoms. He takes his medicines from a weekly organizer. He now smokes about three cigars a day and drinks every day, less than before the stroke. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Since the stroke</td><td>Back at full work; no new neurological symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls since the near-fall in July</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Adherent with a weekly organizer; no new over-the-counter medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Recovering lacunar stroke, hypertension, and cigar smoking</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities of daily living; modified Rankin Scale 1</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and improving since the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Married; large family and staff; mood good; work stress high but welcome</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>About three cigars a day; drinks daily, two or three drinks on most days; little planned exercise apart from walking; sleeps late and naps after lunch</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in bathing, dressing, eating, toileting, and transfers</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages his medicines with an organizer; staff handle his correspondence and travel</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Grab bar fitted in the bathroom after the stroke; good lighting on the stairs; smoke detectors working</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No hearing concerns; reading glasses; last eye examination more than a year ago</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>Gets up once at night to pass urine; no leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns; MoCA improved</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

