<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed, personalized prevention plan updated, and a copy given. Depression, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative; the alcohol screen remains positive. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lacunar stroke about four months ago (I69.354)</content>. Good recovery: modified Rankin Scale 1 at three months and MoCA 27, up from 26 at intake. [S]<list><item>Continue clopidogrel and atorvastatin.</item><item>Stroke review in about three months with a basic metabolic panel.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension (I10)</content>. Blood pressure 124/72 mmHg, at goal, without orthostatic symptoms. [S]<list><item>No change.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, cigars (F17.290)</content>. Down from six to eight cigars a day to about three; not ready to stop. [S]<list><item>Advice to stop repeated; nicotine replacement offered again and declined; revisit at each visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unhealthy alcohol use</content>. AUDIT-C 5, down from 8 at intake. He no longer drinks six or more drinks on one occasion but has more than two drinks on most days; he does not meet criteria for an alcohol use disorder. [S]<list><item>Brief intervention repeated: no more than two drinks a day, with alcohol-free days.</item><item>AUDIT-C at each review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 1953-1954</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 1953-1954</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age; he will have it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 about four years ago; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Single dose about two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed about seven years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about eight and a half years ago; next due in about a year and a half</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 3</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening and counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 5; brief counseling given</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About three cigars a day; advice to stop and an offer of nicotine replacement, declined</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>MoCA 27 of 30</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; outpatient physical therapy completed last month</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL cholesterol 58 mg/dL in August; HbA1c 5.5% in July</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 78 with normal screening in the past; after discussion he declines further screening</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 70</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended only for men aged 65 to 75 who have smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Eligibility is based on cigarette pack-years; he has smoked cigars only</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>More than a year since his last examination; he will book with his optometrist</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 1953-1954 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Stroke and blood pressure review in about three months with a basic metabolic panel. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

